WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.830
If Venom's success the first time around was
largely due to the elements of surprise and

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.420
strangeness, what could the second one have
up its sleeve?

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.960
A lot, potentially.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:13.540
While the law of diminishing returns runs
rampant in Hollywood sequels, Venom 2 could

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.360
actually improve upon its predecessor.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.480
Making Venom the center of his own franchise
presents Sony with some unique challenges

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:21.400
and possibilities.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:25.820
After all, it's not very often that a comic
book character who's usually a villain or

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:29.460
an anti-hero becomes the protagonist of a
comic book franchise.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:33.460
Luckily for Sony, Venom has a nemesis of his
own: Carnage.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.660
Carnage entered the Marvel Universe in the
early '90s, when writer David Michelinie came

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:42.020
up with the idea of a symbiote stripped of
Venom's moral code.

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:47.980
Along with artist Erik Larsen, he introduced
Cletus Kasady, a deranged serial killer and

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:49.760
Eddie Brock's prison cellmate.

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.900
After coming into contact with some of Venom's
drippings, Kasady became Carnage, a blood-red

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:58.120
monster that's fought both Venom and Spider-Man
over the years.

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:03.140
Needless to say, Carnage creeping to the big
screen in Venom 2 will make for a wild ride.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.440
Carnage's appearance in the Venom sequel was
promised by the movie's mid-credits sequence.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:12.120
If you got up and left the theater as soon
as that Eminem song kicked in, you missed

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:16.100
a performance with the potential to match
Tom Hardy's in fearless weirdness.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:21.280
Eddie Brock is sent to a prison to interview
notorious serial killer Cletus Kasady, played

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.359
by Woody Harrelson:

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:29.940
"When I get outta here, and I will, there's
gonna be carnage."

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:34.850
The Venom Blu-ray offered an extended version
of this scene, giving Harrelson a little extra

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:36.120
time to make an impression:

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:40.380
"Talk about sucking out their eyeballs.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.880
Crunchy on the outside."

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:49.700
With Harrelson's history of going all-out
as mesmerizingly unstable characters in movies

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:55.119
like Natural Born Killers and Seven Psychopaths,
Harrelson's expanded role in Venom 2 promises

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:57.880
to push it even more over-the-top than its
predecessor.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:03.760
Sony's plans to explore the dark corners of
Spider-Man's world go beyond Venom and Carnage.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:09.000
In 2018, the studio made the somewhat left-field
announcement that Jared Leto would be starring

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.000
in Morbius.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.540
For those unfamiliar, Morbius the Living Vampire
has been a Spider-Man supporting character

00:02:14.549 --> 00:02:19.360
since the '70s, although he really came into
his own during the same '90s goth craze that

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.640
propelled Venom to stardom.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:25.780
Very little is known about the plot of the
Morbius movie, but Sony is pretty much guaranteed

00:02:25.780 --> 00:02:29.820
to link these two antiheroes in their effort
to keep up in the "Cinematic Universe" game.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.620
The possible introduction of vampires into
Sony's Spider-Verse opens up some intriguing

00:02:34.629 --> 00:02:39.530
new supernatural doorways for Venom 2, even
if Eddie Brock can't hold a candle to our

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:40.700
favorite vampire hunter:

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.540
"You give Frost a message for me.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.580
You tell him it's open season on all suckheads."

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:53.299
We know that a Venom sequel is coming, and
that Tom Hardy and Woody Harrelson are contracted

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.060
to star, but that's really all we know for
certain.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.810
Jeff Pinkner, co-writer of the first movie,
couldn't confirm any more than that in a recent

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.019
interview with the Discussing Film YouTube
channel.

00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.720
"I can't say anything other than that it is
happening."

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:07.400
"Okay, it's happening.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.120
Are you writing it?"

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:11.500
"I am not."

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.610
But while that was all the writer could say
with certainty, he did drop one other major

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:16.280
statement

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:24.080
“It is not impossible that in a future or
upcoming Venom movie that Spider-Man will

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.150
play a significant role."

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:30.730
With Sony's rapidly expanding Spider-Verse,
a potential cameo by the webhead could take

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:31.640
many forms.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.080
Maybe Tom Holland's MCU Peter Parker would
swing by, or perhaps another alternate universe

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.700
incarnation would be the foil to Hardy's Eddie
Brock.

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:43.580
Regardless, a crossover would be sure to get
fans' senses tingling.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.620
Superhero origins can be complicated.

00:03:46.820 --> 00:03:50.840
That's why comics history is so full of reboots,
retcons, and reimaginings.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:54.140
It's also why the plot of the Venom movie
was sometimes messy.

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.060
Take a look at most reviews, and you'll find
that the story structure is one of the most

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.820
commonly criticized elements.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.660
Sometimes, superhero sequels are stronger
than their predecessors.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.740
Captain America: The Winter Soldier outshone
The First Avenger, Thor: Ragnarok proved that

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.800
the third time can be the charm, and The Dark
Knight unquestionably topped Batman Begins.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:18.840
Done right, Venom 2 has the perfect opportunity
to address the first movie's biggest issues.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:24.080
Even the negative reviews of Venom tended
to dish out some positive comments about Tom

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.820
Hardy's bizarre dual performance as Eddie
Brock and Venom.

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:31.560
It's no surprise that Venom appealed to a
performer as adventurous as Tom Hardy.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.600
After all, the job required him to tackle
the primal acting challenge of performing

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:37.500
two-person dialogues with himself.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:42.200
In fact, he may have had a little too much
fun to fit in the movie, as he revealed during

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.920
the press junket that much of his favorite
material didn't make the final cut.

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:50.080
“There are about 30 or 40 minutes worth
of scenes that aren't in this movie."

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.080
"Those are your favorites, right?"

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.420
"All of them, yeah."

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:56.900
Although trimming down a film's more indulgent
passages is a normal part of the filmmaking

00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.580
process, it's hard not to wonder how entertaining
all those scenes of Hardy enjoying himself

00:05:01.580 --> 00:05:02.080
would be.

00:05:02.580 --> 00:05:07.110
Now that it's clear what a strong asset his
eccentric choices were in the first movie,

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.420
maybe the sequel will give him even more room
to play.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.380
"And I have proof!"

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.440
In his review for That Shelf, critic Victor
Shiff said,

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:26.510
"Venom feels like several competing films
— a Jekyll and Hyde story, an odd couple

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:30.420
movie, a broad comedy — stitched together
into one incoherent mess."

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.740
It's hard to completely disagree.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.760
Gritty violence, emotional melodrama, and
wacky sci-fi goofs are all held together within

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.200
the movie's gooey structure.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:43.820
Even when the individual elements make for
a fun ride, it sometimes feels like a movie

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:47.140
that isn't quite sure what kind of total picture
it's going for.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:51.740
Of course, some of that tonal dissonance could
be considered an accurate reflection of Eddie

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:56.020
Brock's splitting psyche as he adjusts to
the idea of playing host to an alien entity.

00:05:56.380 --> 00:06:01.260
And let's not forget that it's basically a
Spider-Man movie without Spider-Man, a pitch

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:04.840
so odd that some uncertainty on the part of
the filmmakers is understandable.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:09.100
Now, though, the creators of the sequel can
look back at the finished product to build

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.540
a stronger foundation to support the next
chapter.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:12.880
"Parasite?"

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.340
"It's a turn of endearment!"

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:16.300
"Apologize!"

00:06:16.420 --> 00:06:17.420
"No."

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.430
"Apologize!"

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.660
"Alright, fine, I'm sorry."

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:25.540
Even during those early days of Venom hype
when no one knew quite what to expect, fans

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.580
always had a checklist of things their favorite
symbiote's big adventure should contain.

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:34.740
A movie about Venom should be dark, it could
definitely get violent, it absolutely must

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.800
get weird, and it could potentially even get
a little kinky.

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:42.410
There was a certain amount of disappointment,
then, when the MPAA slapped the finished product

00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:44.560
with a crowd-friendly PG-13.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:49.020
Now that Venom has proven successful enough
to get a sequel, Sony might also consider

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:51.060
it worth investing in a more niche film.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:56.520
Even if Venom 2 is another PG-13 outing, more
intense footage could be saved for an alternate

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.520
home video cut.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:03.020
Like it or not, fans romantically shipping
Eddie Brock and Venom was inevitable.

00:07:03.140 --> 00:07:07.380
It's no surprise that a movie as bizarre and
meme-worthy as Venom would inspire fans to

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:12.140
spend way too much time thinking about the
bond between its two intertwined main characters.

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:16.960
Whether you see it as an interstellar buddy
movie, a strangely star-crossed rom-com, or

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:22.190
a very particular kind of fetish story, it's
undeniable that much of Venom's charm is in

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.220
the interplay between a boy and his blob.

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.800
"I am putting my hands up."

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.560
"You are making us look bad."

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:31.180
“No I am not!"

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.360
"Yes you are!"

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.400
"No I'm not!"

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:36.220
Of course, it took a long time for these two
to become one.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:40.820
Much of the movie was dedicated to introducing
Eddie, setting up the symbiote's arrival on

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:45.040
Earth, contriving their accidental encounter,
and running them through the trials of their

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:45.540
partnership.

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:50.220
It wasn't until the story neared its climax
that they really started working together,

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:53.520
finally blossoming into the weird little family
they were meant to be.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:58.640
The sequel can take their relationship to
new levels… maybe even some weird levels.

00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.220
"Like a turd in the wind.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.200
Do you feel me?"

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.720
"What the hell are you?"

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.760
"We are Venom."

